# The step of a walk over a Map or a Set in fast code reads in line the keys of the width that the type of the keys promises; a table with keys of the other width is for the stub that stands in front of the operation.
# A number never fits a short key: numbers (beside undefined, null and booleans, which fit both) are read as wide keys, keys that are never numbers as short ones. Where the keys may be numbers or something else, both widths are read in line.
# The sizes tell the three forms apart: every walk of one form is as long as the first of that form, and no two forms are as long as each other.
# FORM: Placed
# OPTIONS: heat=OnlyLoopsAreHot check=validate-back-end
# RUN: generate-code calls
# RUN(W): generate-code calls
# RUN(B): generate-code calls
# RUN(S): code-shapes

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js"
function f0 name="texts" parameters=[{type=Set<string>}, {type=anything}, {type=i32}] results=[{type=anything}] {
    Jump -> next b1()
  b1():
    LoopHint
    v4 = SetNext v0, v1, v2
    v5 = ResultAt v4
    v6 = ResultAt v4 index=2
    Branch v5 -> taken b1(), notTaken b2()
  b2():
    Return v6
}
# CHECK: f0: size=[[short]] frame=
# CHECK-NOT: size=[[short]] frame=
# S: f0 b1 Fast

